#: includes/class-fkhs-privacy.php:37
msgid "The H5P → Sensei Bridge stores user, lesson and activity identifiers, a lesson title snapshot, scores, completion/pass flags, event identifiers, a payload hash and the stored site time. By default it also retains the submitted xAPI statement, which may include names, email addresses, answers and contextual data. Administrators can configure future raw-statement storage and explicitly clear older raw statements without removing progress. Attempts are retained by default, including after deactivation, uninstall or account deletion. WordPress personal-data tools can export attempts for an existing account; erasure requires explicit site policy approval and may change H5P completion requirements. Set your retention period and coordinate erasure with Sensei, backups and any external stores."
msgstr ""

